{
  "schema": "muse-workflow-graph/v1",
  "id": "flow-telegram-ai-bot-with-langchain-nodes-7c5263",
  "title": "Telegram AI bot with LangChain nodes",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "step-1",
      "label": "OpenAI Chat Model",
      "operation": "model",
      "adapter": "model",
      "parameters": {
        "capability": "text generation",
        "settings": {
          "temperature": 0.7,
          "frequencyPenalty": 0.2
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "step-2",
      "label": "Window Buffer Memory",
      "operation": "session",
      "adapter": "session-store",
      "parameters": {
        "sessionKey": {
          "expression": "chat_with_{{ steps[\"step-6\"].records[0].message.chat.id }}"
        },
        "contextWindowLength": 10
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "step-3",
      "label": "Telegram",
      "operation": "service-write",
      "adapter": "telegram",
      "parameters": {
        "text": {
          "expression": "{{ record.output }}"
        },
        "chatId": {
          "expression": "{{ steps[\"step-6\"].records[0].message.from.id }}"
        },
        "additionalFields": {
          "parse_mode": "HTML",
          "appendAttribution": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "step-4",
      "label": "Correct errors",
      "operation": "service-write",
      "adapter": "telegram",
      "parameters": {
        "text": {
          "expression": "{{ steps[\"step-11\"].record.output.replace(/&/g, \"&amp;\").replace(/>/g, \"&gt;\").replace(/</g, \"&lt;\").replace(/\"/g, \"&quot;\") }}"
        },
        "chatId": {
          "expression": "{{ steps[\"step-6\"].records[0].message.from.id }}"
        },
        "additionalFields": {
          "parse_mode": "HTML",
          "appendAttribution": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "step-5",
      "label": "Execute Workflow Trigger",
      "operation": "input",
      "adapter": "muse",
      "parameters": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "step-6",
      "label": "Listen for incoming events",
      "operation": "input",
      "adapter": "muse",
      "parameters": {
        "updates": [
          "message"
        ],
        "additionalFields": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "step-7",
      "label": "Send back an image",
      "operation": "service-write",
      "adapter": "telegram",
      "parameters": {
        "file": {
          "expression": "{{ record.data[0].url }}"
        },
        "chatId": {
          "expression": "{{ steps[\"step-5\"].records[0].chat_id }}"
        },
        "operation": "sendPhoto",
        "additionalFields": {
          "parse_mode": "HTML"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "step-8",
      "label": "add response field",
      "operation": "map-fields",
      "adapter": "local",
      "parameters": {
        "fields": {
          "values": [
            {
              "name": "response",
              "stringValue": "Success"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "step-9",
      "label": "Dall-E 3 Tool",
      "operation": "service-read",
      "adapter": "workflow",
      "parameters": {
        "name": "Draw_Dalle_image",
        "fields": {
          "values": [
            {
              "name": "chat_id",
              "stringValue": {
                "expression": "{{ steps[\"step-6\"].records[0].message.chat.id }}"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        "workflowId": {
          "expression": "{{ workflow_id }}"
        },
        "description": "Call this tool to request a Dall-E 3 model, when the user asks to draw something. Please send the user request for an image as an inline query string."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "step-10",
      "label": "Generate image in Dall-E 3",
      "operation": "http",
      "adapter": "http",
      "parameters": {
        "url": {
          "configuration_input": "step-10-url"
        },
        "method": "POST",
        "options": {},
        "sendBody": true,
        "bodyParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "model",
              "value": "dall-e-3"
            },
            {
              "name": "prompt",
              "value": {
                "expression": "{{ record.query }}"
              }
            },
            {
              "name": "n",
              "value": 1
            },
            {
              "name": "size",
              "value": "1024x1024"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "step-11",
      "label": "AI Agent",
      "operation": "generate",
      "adapter": "model",
      "parameters": {
        "text": {
          "expression": "{{ record.message.text }}"
        },
        "options": {
          "humanMessage": {
            "expression": "TOOLS\n------\nAssistant can ask the user to use tools to look up information that may be helpful in answering the users original question. The tools the human can use are:\n\n{tools}\n\n{format_instructions}\n\nUSER'S INPUT\n--------------------\nHere is the user's input (remember to respond with a markdown code snippet of a json blob with a single action, and NOTHING else):\n\n{{input}}"
          },
          "systemMessage": {
            "expression": "You are a helpful AI assistant. You are chatting with the user named `{{ record.message.from.first_name }}`. Today is {{ DateTime.fromISO(current_time).toLocaleString(DateTime.DATETIME_FULL) }}\n\nFrom time to time call a user by name (if the user name is provided). In your reply, always send a message in Telegram-supported HTML format. Here are the formatting instructions:\n1. The following tags are currently supported:\n<b>bold</b>, <strong>bold</strong>\n<i>italic</i>, <em>italic</em>\n<u>underline</u>, <ins>underline</ins>\n<s>strikethrough</s>, <strike>strikethrough</strike>, <del>strikethrough</del>\n<span class=\"tg-spoiler\">spoiler</span>, <tg-spoiler>spoiler</tg-spoiler>\n<b>bold <i>italic bold <s>italic bold strikethrough <span class=\"tg-spoiler\">italic bold strikethrough spoiler</span></s> <u>underline italic bold</u></i> bold</b>\n<a href=\"http://www.example.com/\">inline URL</a>\n<code>inline fixed-width code</code>\n<pre>pre-formatted fixed-width code block</pre>\n2. Any code that you send should be wrapped in these tags: <pre><code class=\"language-python\">pre-formatted fixed-width code block written in the Python programming language</code></pre>\nOther programming languages are supported as well.\n3. All <, > and & symbols that are not a part of a tag or an HTML entity must be replaced with the corresponding HTML entities (< with &lt;, > with &gt; and & with &amp;)\n4. If the user sends you a message starting with / sign, it means this is a Telegram bot command. For example, all users send /start command as their first message. Try to figure out what these commands mean and reply accodringly"
          }
        }
      }
    }
  ],
